infographic list-zigzag-down-simple
data
  title enableImplicitConversion: one flag, four silent mis-coercions
  desc Coerce-by-type, not by-value — each query string becomes a wrong value, and no 400 is raised
  lists
    - label ?active=false  →  true
      desc boolean field: Boolean('false') is a non-empty string, so truthy — the show-deactivated filter inverts
    - label ?page= (empty)  →  0
      desc number field: Number('') is 0, a silent default page slips through
    - label ?page=12abc  →  NaN
      desc number field: Number('12abc') is NaN, passed straight into the query
    - label ?ids=  →  coercion guesses
      desc array field: a validation boundary should reject, not guess
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #6366f1
